Does anybody have the FSF/GNU's gcc 2.8.0 up and running on VMS?

I'm trying to help some customers accomplish this.  We have gcc 2.7.2
running on VAX VMS 6.1.
We have gcc 2.8.0 running successfully on Solaris and HP/UX.  On the
VAX, however,
there seem to be pieces missing.  My customers built gcc 2.7.2
themselves when it was new,
so we're all familiar with the process.  The FSF docs say to use
install.com, which is not in any copy
of the gcc 2.8.0 archive I have found.  We attempted to hack the
install.com from the gcc 2.7.2
release, which we used successfully to build that version, but we get
large numbers of
compile errors that way.

I've looked at the VMS ftp sites that I know of, but everybody I can
find is still offering version 2.7.x.
The FSF CD-ROM in the past has sometimes not included the most current
pieces for VMS.
Does anybody know the most reliable way to get working executables, get
the missing pieces to
build a executables, or get a packaged release that is guaranteed to
have all the correct pieces
we need to run gcc 2.8.0 on our VAXen?

Thanks in advance for any information.

