Doug Mallory wrote:
> 
> I have a weird problem on a site, and can't figure out how this is
> happening. During a day, several files are created, with print data in them,
> without being in a directory. After a ana/disk/repair I get these files in
> the syslost directory, all names   .dat;*.
> How can this happen without something complaining, and how can these files
> even get created this way, and of course, how do I fix it?

Sounds like printer spool files, not knowing any better. Do you have a
printer set /SPOOLED? If an application opens such a printer directly,
the output is redirected to a file. On close, the file is submitted to
the appropriate queue for printing. Such files are not entered in any
directory as a performance optimization. They'll show up as lost files
if you do an ANALYZE/DISK/REPAIR while they're open or while the print
jobs are pending. Assuming your queue manager and printer are working
correctly, they should go away by themselves when the print jobs
complete.



