> even get created this way, and of course, how do I fix it?

Can you provide a sample set of names (beyond "*.dat")?  And perhaps a
snippet of the contents of one of them?

This is perfectly permissible and supported; it sounds as though some
application is setting FAB$V_TMP when it really meant to use FAB$V_TMD.
Or perhaps the creating process' default protection mask doesn't
provide delete access to the owner, which might keep the "d" part of
TMD from functioning.

The real key is to find out what the creating application is - hopefully
the answers to the questions above will help narrow it down.

