Hi,

I was very happy today, getting one of the very first "au" series machines
under my desk. Very zippy; little bit too big/heavy for my taste.
After a while my happyness almost passed away (nevertheless still excited)
after I ran into serious problems:

So far I had no experience with DECnet V. There was no need for it, DECnet
IV worked perfectly. VMS 7.1 seems not to support the old DECnet IV any more
:-(. After I managed to get it configured I was looking desperately for an
equivalent to:
"mc ncp copy known nodes from MYNODE to both"
"mc ncp set/def node OTHER address 49.666"
...nothing

After a while jumping through "mc ncl help" and "help" I gave up very
frustrated. Now a huge stack of Documentation about DECnet-Plus for OpenVMS
is sitting in front of me; very depressing.

The second problem came up with UCX and an dns lookup. In our network a
WinNT server does a pretty good job as a DNS server. With VMS 6.2 and UCX
4.1 there were no problems at all (if you forget about the ucx sh host error
message). With the new machine the exact same configuration does not work
any more. The only clue I have is that DECnet/OSI might fuck arround in my
ucx name service.

The last kick came, when I tried to compile my programms. I installed the
very last verison of the C compiler (5.6 from the NOV 97 release of the
Layered Products). I thought new is new. But a lot of the pthread library
functions have changed names os do not exist any more... pages of compile
errors |-{. I feel totally bummed. In the past, DEC was very careful with
changing interfaces, that was one reason I was promoting VMS.

This was my short storry, now let me ask for some assistance to help
restoring my faith in OpenVMS and DEC.

DECnet V:
