First, I would like to thank all how responded, My first reaction was,
stupid me..of course these are from a spooled device scratch file.
But the next question, then was why didn't they disappear after
printing...Well I found the offending app., which was printing directly to a
LAT service, spooled to the system disk. The application was using a blank
file name and .dat ext in its qio to the output device. Best guess here is
the system couldn't delete the bad file name. Fix one was unspool the
device. Then after that fix the app so no filename was used..Looks to be
fine now.

The O/S is v6.1, if that helps, no ECO's that I know of have been installed.

Thanks again.  Doug.





